                        "entry_id": "a519c40c-6c11-3590-b15e-1d4169eea4eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Corps astrophysique en équilibre hydrostatique pas assez massif pour être un fuseur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7d74e0c-f570-43e1-bf82-1fdc30f3eeb1",
                                "sense_id": "f45e2ba9-afff-3f33-8b36-9b97aa21dce8",
                                "text": "Certains planémos isolés peuvent errer dans l’espace interstellaire sans jamais orbiter autour d’une étoile."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e12de15-adf2-41b4-826c-fd4391cba25f",
                                "sense_id": "f45e2ba9-afff-3f33-8b36-9b97aa21dce8",
                                "text": "Les planémos comprennent les planètes, les planètes naines et les plus grandes lunes du système solaire, mais aussi les planètes errantes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "43a8bd3d-fc2c-417a-8dd9-ccaf0c3a54ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "a519c40c-6c11-3590-b15e-1d4169eea4eb",
                        "source_sense_id": "f45e2ba9-afff-3f33-8b36-9b97aa21dce8",
                        "target_lang_word": "planemo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "planemo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a45350ba-240e-3f52-8c8d-53152ab3e3b5",
                                        "entry_id": "519c1773-632c-3c84-8102-5c79ac0a66c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "an astronomical object with enough mass to achieve hydrostatic equilibrium, but not enough to initiate core fusion at any time in its existence. That is, it is rounded in shape and is smaller than a star. Planemos include planets, dwarf planets, and the larger moons of the Solar System (satellite planets), but also sub-brown dwarfs and rogue planets between the stars."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3081d42d-61f4-4a50-a0d4-7d10355e372d",
                                                "sense_id": "a45350ba-240e-3f52-8c8d-53152ab3e3b5",
                                                "text": "Other groups have also recently identified young, isolated planemos; understanding how such isolated, ultra-low masses form presents a challenge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
